    "https://www.methodist.edu/offices-services/human-resources/positions-available/": {
      "title": "Secondary",
      "description": "Positions Available | Human Resources | Methodist University Skip Main Navigation Skip to site alert Secondary Apply Request Info Visit Giving Methodist University Menu Secondary Apply Request Info Visit Giving For You Close For You Prospective Students Newly Admitted Students Current Students Online Students Military & Veteran Students International Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Menu Search You are here: Home Offices & Services Human Resources Positions Available Positions Available Positions Available Dear visitors, Methodist University is a wonderful place to work and we are fortunate to have talented faculty and staff to enrich our student experience and provide high-quality education and services to our students. MU is a vibrant community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators who live, study, and work together. This process of sharing experiences offers the opportunity for each of us to be more knowledgeable and productive than we would be alone, as well as caring citizens within our community. Sincerely, Stanley T. Wearden, Ph.D. President Positions Available In addition to open positions at Methodist University (which includes positions with the School of Medicine) , MU is also highlighting jobs at Cape Fear Valley Health that have an affiliation with the School of Medicine. You must apply for these jobs through the CFVH link/system. Positions at Methodist University Jobs available at Methodist University, including the School of Medicine Positions at Cape Fear Valley Health Open positions with Cape Fear Valley Health affiliated with the School of Medicine, such as the Hospitalist (Academic Faculty) position EOE/ADA Compliance Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We consider all applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), we provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. If you need assistance or an accommodation during the application or hiring process, please contact Human Resources at [email protected] . H‑1B Sponsorship Information The University values the contributions of international scholars and supports employment‑based sponsorship where possible. At this time, the University is unable to initiate H‑1B petitions for individuals located outside the United States who would require consular processing. For candidates already in the U.S., the University may consider the following H‑1B actions: Change of Status (COS) Change of Employer (COE) Candidates working in the U.S. on valid OPT may be eligible for H‑1B sponsorship through a Change of Status after review of immigration documentation and qualifications. All other sponsorship requests are reviewed on a case‑by‑case basis in consultation with immigration counsel. Methodist University Location 5400 Ramsey Street Fayetteville, NC 28311 910.630.7000 Helpful Links Maps & Directions Parking Information Emergency Information Employment News Event Calendar Connect With Us Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Title IX Consumer Information © Methodist University 2026 Site Menu Search Submit Site Explore MU In Brief In Our Own Words In Pictures In the World In Athletics In Our Local Community In the Numbers Our Value On a Tour About MU About Our Relationship to the United Methodist Church A Brief History of Methodist University The Arts at MU Offices & Services Our Mission Strategic Initiatives Careers at MU Accreditation Event Rentals Leadership Academics Academic Programs (On-Campus & Online) Methodist University Online Davis Memorial Library One Stop Academic Calendars & Schedules Academic Catalog Registrar Graduation Educational Centers Faculty & Staff Awar