    "https://www.methodist.edu/academics/awards/": {
      "title": "Secondary",
      "description": "Awards | Academics | Methodist University Skip Main Navigation Skip to site alert Secondary Apply Request Info Visit Giving Methodist University Menu Secondary Apply Request Info Visit Giving For You Close For You Prospective Students Newly Admitted Students Current Students Online Students Military & Veteran Students International Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Menu Search You are here: Home Academics Awards Faculty & Staff Awards Faculty & Staff Awards 2027 Faculty & Staff Awards I encourage you to take a few moments to review our teaching and service awards and to nominate deserving colleagues. Please also encourage your students to submit nominees for the awards. Descriptions and criteria, lists of past winners, and nomination forms are available for each award on the web page below. Nominations close February 15, 2027. The earlier nomination and selection process this year will allow us to announce winners at the Awards Ceremony on Symposium Day on April 7, 2027. We will also celebrate winners at a reception during the Start-of-Semester Faculty Development Conference in August 2027. Thank you for taking time to recognize our fabulous faculty and staff, Suzanne Blum Malley Provost Nominations Nominations for the faculty and staff awards are accepted from December 1 to February 15 each year, and the awards are presented at the Student Awards Celebration on Symposium Day. For more information please see the awards descriptions and nomination forms below: Award Descriptions, Winners & Nomination Forms Distinguished Professor of the Year Award Every year, Methodist University honors a full-time faculty member who has made a distinct difference in the teaching climate of the university. Criteria Previous Winners Nomination Form Alfred E. Cleveland Award for Excellence in Teaching A faculty member must have completed three full academic years of full-time teaching at Methodist University before being eligible for consideration, and at least three full academic years must elapse before a prior recipient is again eligible for consideration. Criteria Previous Winners Nomination Form Faculty Mentoring & Service Award We encourage nominations of faculty who go above and beyond to nurture meaningful connections, a sense of belonging, and embodying Methodist University’s dedication to student success and institutional excellence. Criteria Previous Winners Nomination Form Staff Mentoring & Service Award We encourage nominations of staff who go above and beyond to nurture meaningful connections, a sense of belonging, and embodying Methodist University’s dedication to student success and institutional excellence. Criteria Previous Winners Nomination Form President’s Award for Faculty Research & Creative Expression Previous Winners Methodist University Location 5400 Ramsey Street Fayetteville, NC 28311 910.630.7000 Helpful Links Maps & Directions Parking Information Emergency Information Employment News Event Calendar Connect With Us Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Title IX Consumer Information © Methodist University 2026 Site Menu Search Submit Site Explore MU In Brief In Our Own Words In Pictures In the World In Athletics In Our Local Community In the Numbers Our Value On a Tour About MU About Our Relationship to the United Methodist Church A Brief History of Methodist University The Arts at MU Offices & Services Our Mission Strategic Initiatives Careers at MU Accreditation Event Rentals Leadership Academics Academic Programs (On-Campus & Online) Methodist University Online Davis Memorial Library One Stop Academic Calendars & Schedules Academic Catalog Registrar Graduation Educational Centers Faculty & Staff Awards Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Financial Aid & Scholarships Admitted Students Athletics Life at MU Get Involved Health & Wellness Housing